// For n <=8 fixed is strictly smaller than either alternative.
// Unique three-byte windows are a sufficient condition for no LZ match.
// The real collector still runs and checks that its cached parse is forced.
optimal-short-triple(input<[u8]>, at<u64>) => (out<u64>) :=
